145	## Using `frai-core` (SDK)
146	
147	Install from npm:
148	```bash
149	pnpm add frai-core
150	```
151	
152	`frai-core` exposes modular helpers that the CLI uses under the hood:
153	- `Questionnaire` – interactive question flows.
154	- `Documents` – generate checklists, model cards, and risk files.
155	- `Scanners` – static analysis for AI indicators.
156	- `Rag` – policy-grounded indexing utilities.
157	- `Eval` – baseline evaluation metrics and report writers.
158	- `Finetune` – governance templates, validation, and readiness scoring.
159	- `Config` & `Providers` – key management and LLM provider wiring.
160	
161	Example: generate documentation programmatically.
162	
163	```ts
164	import fs from 'fs/promises';
165	import inquirer from 'inquirer';
166	import { Documents, Questionnaire, Scanners } from 'frai-core';
167	
168	const answers = await Questionnaire.runQuestionnaire({
169	  prompt: (questions) => inquirer.prompt(questions)
170	});
171	
172	const { checklist, modelCard, riskFile } = Documents.generateDocuments({ answers });
173	const scan = Scanners.scanCodebase({ root: process.cwd() });
174	const aiContext = Documents.buildContextForAITips(answers);
175	
176	await fs.writeFile('checklist.md', checklist);
177	await fs.writeFile('model_card.md', modelCard);
178	await fs.writeFile('risk_file.md', riskFile);
